\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. What are these arrayed in white,
\par Brighter than the noonday sun?
\par Foremost of the sons of light,
\par Nearest the eternal throne?
\par These are they that bore the cross,
\par Nobly for their Master stood;
\par Sufferers in His righteous cause,
\par Followers of the dying God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Out of great distress they came,
\par Washed their robes by faith below
\par In the blood of yonder Lamb,
\par Blood that washes white as snow:
\par Therefore are they next the throne.
\par Serve their Maker day and night;
\par God resides among His own,
\par God doth in His saints delight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. More than conquerors at last,
\par Here they find their trials o'er;
\par They have all their sufferings past,
\par Hunger now and thirst no more;
\par No excessive heat they feel
\par From the sun's directer ray,
\par In a milder clime they dwell,
\par Region of eternal day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He that on the throne doth reign,
\par Them the Lamb shall always feed,
\par With the tree of life sustain,
\par To the living fountains lead;
\par He shall all their sorrows chase,
\par All their wants at once remove,
\par Wipe the tears from every face,
\par Fill up every soul with love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

